;; FUSE-NF §4.3.5 Autoencoder Analysis — FAITHFUL arm — readable MeTTa RENDERING
;; Never loaded: a unit is a conjunctive query over variables, not an assertion. The record of truth is
;;   ae_faithful.jsonl (adopted k / beta) and ae_faithful_dial/k<k>_beta<b>.jsonl   (every pair with cosine >= 0.8)
;;   ae_faithful_weights/k<k>_beta<b>_seed<s>.tsv   (one encoder weight vector per unit)
;;
;; BLOCK: bottleneck 16, sparsity beta 0.5, gate cosine >= 0.85 — one point of the dial; the adopted setting (k 32, beta 0.5, cosine 0.85) is
;;   ../ae_faithful.metta
;;
;; PARAMETERS (choices the paper leaves open; disclosed)
;;   units           out_h/patterns2_faithful.jsonl: 1454 rooted-subtree units of the §4.3.1 faithful view, taken as-is
;;                   (subsumed units and identical columns included — the faithful arm never pre-filters)
;;   records         canonical_substrate.jsonl: 2302 records
;;   vectorisation   count of each unit's matches (variable bindings) per record, recounted with the miner's enumerator
;;                   (k = 4 atoms, 28 eligible atoms per record, surface atoms excluded, constants verbatim)
;;                   and verified against the inventory (column sums = occurrences, non-zero rows = support sets);
;;                   raw counts, no scaling: 11330 non-zero cells, 1075 repeat matches beyond the first
;;   autoencoder     one hidden layer of 16 sigmoid units, linear output, tied decoder x_hat = h W + c;
;;                   init W uniform(+-sqrt(6/(F+k))), b = 0, c = the column means
;;   loss            mean over records of the squared reconstruction error summed over units + 0.0001 ||W||^2
;;                   + beta 0.5 * sum_j KL(rho 0.1 || mean activation of hidden unit j)   (beta 0 = the plain shallow AE)
;;   training        full batch, Adam lr 0.01, 2000 epochs, float32, 8 thread(s), seed 0 adopted;
;;                   seeds 0..4 retrain the same model for the stability count
;;                   this block: reconstruction 3.5725 per record, R^2 0.4179, mean activation 0.102
;;   ties            cosine between the two units' encoder weight vectors (the columns of W, 16-dimensional);
;;                   gate cosine >= 0.85 (dial 0.80, 0.85, 0.90, 0.95); recording floor 0.8
;;   co-occurrence   from the units' record sets: exclusive (no shared record) / overlapping / nested / same-records;
;;                   part-of = one unit's atoms embed in the other's (§4.3.1 containment) — a FIELD, never a filter
;;   tie groups      complete linkage on the cosine distance of the weight vectors, cut at 1 - tau: every pair inside a
;;                   group passes the gate; a partition (a unit sits in one group) — the pairwise record is the JSONL
;;
;; RECORD FORMAT (every record is one pair, with its gate verdict)
;;   ;; [relation(, part-of)]  A ~ B   cosine <seed 0> (seeds <n>/<S> >= tau)   records <A> / <B> / <shared>   norms <A> / <B>   gate: PASS|FAIL
;;   ;;   A: <query A>   e.g. <witness record ids>
;;   ;;   B: <query B>
;;   (Implication <B> <A>)
;;     = the consolidation as the rule it would become: the minority unit (smaller support) rewrites to the majority
;;     unit; variables as each unit's own canonical naming (an exclusive pair shares no record, so no alignment
;;     is observable); naming and direction provisional, the gauntlet decides. Rendered for PASS and FAIL alike.
;; A is the unit with the larger support (tie: query order). PASS pairs grouped by relation — EXCLUSIVE first (the
;; paper's interchangeability reading: the two units never share a record), then OVERLAPPING, NESTED and SAME-RECORDS
;; (co-occurrence: these restate §4.3.3 / §4.3.1 and are corroboration, not new rules) — each group by cosine;
;; near misses are in the JSONL (every pair at or above the recording floor).

;; ==================== TIED PAIRS: 14165 pass the gate — exclusive 4245, overlapping 3251, nested 4262, same-records 2407 — among the 1056331 pairs of 1454 units; 18190 pairs recorded in the JSONL ====================

;; [exclusive]  p204174 ~ p206538   cosine 1.0000 (seeds 5/5 >= 0.85)   records 4 / 3 / 0   norms 0.01 / 0.01   gate: PASS
;;   A: (Inheritance regional_unit regional)   e.g. tierC-000031 tierC-000032 tierC-000249 tierC-000250
;;   B: (And (Inheritance metropolitan_statistical_area area) (Inheritance metropolitan_statistical_area metropolitan))
(Implication (And (Inheritance metropolitan_statistical_area area) (Inheritance metropolitan_statistical_area metropolitan)) (Inheritance regional_unit regional))

;; [exclusive]  p204175 ~ p206592   cosine 1.0000 (seeds 5/5 >= 0.85)   records 4 / 3 / 0   norms 0.01 / 0.01   gate: PASS
;;   A: (Inheritance regional_unit unit)   e.g. tierC-000031 tierC-000032 tierC-000249 tierC-000250
;;   B: (Inheritance metropolitan_statistical_area metropolitan)
(Implication (Inheritance metropolitan_statistical_area metropolitan) (Inheritance regional_unit unit))

;; [exclusive]  p207668 ~ p207689   cosine 1.0000 (seeds 5/5 >= 0.85)   records 3 / 3 / 0   norms 0.01 / 0.01   gate: PASS
;;   A: (Member $x0 beach)   e.g. tierB-000221 tierB-001081 tierB-000949 tierB-001232
;;   B: (Member $x0 fact)
